From eb87442860ee42e8b23644b08aed2ea63fabff89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:07:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-113293: Use after free in ANGLE

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8427126:
HLSL: Fix name collision due to lack of delimiter

The HLSL names were generated as `nameID`, which could collide with a
different name ending with a prefix of `ID` and an ID that's the suffix
of `ID`, for example `a` with ID `13579` and `a1` with id `3579`.

This change removes the possibility of collisions by producing names
like `name_ID`, which aligns with how the IR produces names.

There is no regression test in this fix because causing such a collision
reliably (across changes to ANGLE, which frequently changes the IDs)
requires too many try and errors in the test to be practical.  Note that
the IDs between the two variables must be at least 10000 apart, given
the translator starts user IDs at 3000.

Bug: chromium:562040486
